CORE
main.cpp
--cpp11
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ initializer_list size: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ initializer_list first element: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ WRONG size \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
N5008 [dcl.init.list]/5: `std::initializer_list<int> il = {1,2,3}` synthesises a
backing `const int[3]` array and makes `il` refer to it.  Fixed by
build_initializer_list_value + routing an explicit initializer_list<E> target to
it in convert_initializer (previously CBMC tried to match the braced list
against initializer_list's own constructors and reported "found no match", which
the unsupported-construct leniency then silently swallowed -- a vacuous pass).
assertion.3 provides non-vacuity.
